{"name":"Waikiki","hex":"#218ba0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Waikiki","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A beachfront neighborhood of Honolulu, Hawaii, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Waikiki"}],"entries":[{"title":"Waikiki (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Waikiki were a rock group from Sydney, Australia, consisting of sister and brother Juanita Stein (bass/vocals) and Joel Stein (guitar/vocals), and Glenn Moule (drums) and Jimmy Brandon (guitar). A new bass player Brendan Picchio joined the band in early 2003, replacing Brandon, with Juanita Stein moving from bass to rhythm guitar. In August 2003, Joel Stein explained the impact Picchio had made on the group. He told Radio Adelaide's Hermione Gilchrist that the new bassist was \"the missing piece to the puzzle\", adding, \"he's what we've been looking for since we started.\""}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waikiki_(band)"},{"title":"Waikiki (1980 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Waikiki is a 1980 American action crime drama television film that originally aired on ABC. Directed by Ron Satlof, it stars Dack Rambo, Steve Marachuk, Donna Mills, Tanya Roberts, Cal Bellini, and Darren McGavin and follows a pair of private detectives called on to investigate the bizarre serial murders of young women in Waikiki. The film combines elements of a crime thriller with the atmosphere of an exotic resort in the 1980s. Despite the serious nature of the plot, the film maintains a light and dynamic atmosphere thanks to the colorful characters and local landscapes."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/09/Waikiki-1980-dvd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waikiki_(1980_film)"},{"title":"Waikīkī","blocks":[{"text":"Waikīkī is a Honolulu neighborhood and the eponymous Waikīkī beach on its south shore, on the island of Oʻahu in the U.S. state of Hawaii."}],"i